  "sn35.116:1.1": "The “end of the world” is taught to brahmin cosmologists at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an9.38/en/sujato'>AN 9.38</a>, and illustrated with the parable of Rohitassa at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn2.26/en/sujato'>SN 2.26</a> = <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.45/en/sujato'>AN 4.45</a>. | I use both “world” and “cosmos” for <i lang='pi' translate='no'>loka</i>. As this discourse shows, the exact meaning is highly mutable and context-specific. ",
